A||N||5||albie1kanobe||oil pressure gauge||||5||
Z||000000||albie1kanobe||08-19-2001||09:07 PM||||I have an '87 SE 6 cyl. auto.  My oil pressure gauge blasts to max when I start up and it stays there until I shut down.  I have no oil problems or known leaks.  Any ideas? Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||08-19-2001||09:14 PM||||replace the sensor. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||albie1kanobe||08-19-2001||09:16 PM||||thanks...and now for the dumb question #2...where exactly is the sensor and what does it look like?||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||09:34 PM||||on the backside of engine block, by the oil filter. its screwed into the block with an electrical connector on top.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||08-19-2001||10:34 PM||||If the car came with factory A/C first look on the top of the engine to the right of the plenum, near the battery tray.   You're more likely to find it there than down near the oil filter. <P>I've posted this link before, but here is a (fairly large) pic of a new sensor before plugging the harness back into the top:<BR> <A HREF="http://fiero.xcom.net/fiero2a.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero.xcom.net/fiero2a.jpg</A> <P>In the upper left of the picture you can just see the edge of the radiator cap and in the lower right you can see the fan belt. <P>This pic is from my '86 SE but the sensor is in the same location on my '87 GT. <P><p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||JetroGT||08-20-2001||02:25 AM||||If it's unpluged it will peg the gauge.||||reg||1
